A service renders a preview by fetching whatever address the caller supplies. All of it is written for this course.

```
app.get('/preview', async (req, res) => {
  const target = req.query.url;
  if (!/^https?:\/\/[a-z0-9.-]+$/i.test(target)) {
    return res.status(400).send('bad url');
  }
  const body = await fetch(target, { timeout: 2000 }).then(r => r.text());
  res.type('html').send(`<iframe src="data:text/html;base64,${b64(body)}">`);
});
```

The service runs inside the network and can reach an internal administration interface. What is the missing control?

A handler writes one line per request. All of it is written for this course.

```
function writeLog(req) {
  const line = `${req.method} ${req.path} ${req.headers['user-agent']} ` +
              `from=${req.socket.remoteAddress} outcome=${res.statusCode}\n`;
  fs.appendFileSync('/var/log/app/access.log', line);
}
```

