A client library used across an internal estate resolves names like this. All of it is written for this course.

```
function resolve(name) {
  const q = buildQuery(name, 'A');        // asks for one record type
  const reply = udpSendOnce(q);            // one attempt, no retry
  for (const record of reply.additional) {
    cache.set(record.name, record);        // stored whatever name is there
  }
  return firstAnswer(reply);
}
```

A party on the network between the client and the resolver sends a reply before the real one arrives. What does the library do?
